# Uninstall and install-state

`cw uninstall` removes shell integration and deletes `$CW_ROOT` (`rm -rf`). Source of truth for reversible host edits: `.state/install-state` (tab-separated).

## Record every host mutation at install time

Use helpers in `lib/state.sh` only. Never silently edit user files.

| Action | API | `install-state` kind | Reversed by `cw_state_reverse`? |
|--------|-----|----------------------|----------------------------------|
| Symlink dotfile | `cw_state_safe_symlink src dest` | `symlink` | Yes: removes symlink |
| Create empty file we own | touch + `cw_state_record create` | `create` | Yes: deletes file |
| Managed block in `~/.bash_aliases` | `cw_state_ensure_managed_block` | `modify` + `backup` | Yes: strips `# >>> cw >>>` block |
| `~/.local/bin/cw` link | `install.sh` | `local-bin-symlink` | Yes (+ hardcoded in uninstall) |
| Download bundled tool | `cw_tools_install_*` | `tool` | No (`rm -rf $CW_ROOT` on uninstall) |
| Bundled tool update timestamp | `cw_state_tool_mark_updated` | (in `.state/tools-updated/`) | No (deleted with `$CW_ROOT`) |
| Crawler list | `.state/crawlers.json` | (in `.state/`) | No (deleted with `$CW_ROOT`) |

If you add a **new** mutation kind, you MUST:

1. Call `cw_state_record <kind> <path> <extra>` during install/update
2. Implement reverse logic in `cw_state_reverse` (new `case` branch) when the path is outside `$CW_ROOT`
3. Append human line to `install.log` via `cw_state_log "..."`

## Logging

- `cw_state_log` -> `.state/install.log` (operator audit; not in shareable reports)
- Log install start/finish, update, collect report id (not full paths in collect log if avoidable)
- Permissions: `.state/` 0700, `install-state` 0600

## Uninstall flow (`cw uninstall` / `uninstall.sh`)

1. `cw_state_reverse` (LIFO over `install-state`)
2. Remove `~/.local/bin/cw` if symlink
3. `rm -rf $CW_ROOT` (tools, shims, `.state`, source)

## Checklist for any install-side change

```
[ ] Mutation goes through cw_state_* helper
[ ] install-state row written when path is outside $CW_ROOT
[ ] install.log line written
[ ] cw_state_reverse handles paths outside $CW_ROOT
[ ] uninstall tested: bash_aliases clean, symlinks gone, cw off PATH, $CW_ROOT removed
[ ] Re-install works after uninstall
```

## Do not break uninstall

- Do not `rm -rf` user paths in diagnostic commands
- Do not add second managed block markers (use `CW_MANAGED_BEGIN` / `CW_MANAGED_END` in `lib/common.sh`)
- Do not write install files outside `$CW_ROOT` without recording them in `install-state`
